[{"input":"{mainmatter=\"start\"}\n# Lecture 1 – Computing Concepts\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\n- Define what a computer is.\n- Distinguish between hardware and software.\n- Explain the input-process-output-storage model.\n- Differentiate between general-purpose computers and embedded systems.\n- Explain the concept of abstraction in computing.\n- Describe the major milestones in the evolution of computing.","output":"","result":"{mainmatter=\"start\"}\n# Lecture 1 – Computing Concepts\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\n- Define what a computer is.\n- Distinguish between hardware and software.\n- Explain the input-process-output-storage model.\n- Differentiate between general-purpose computers and embedded systems.\n- Explain the concept of abstraction in computing.\n- Describe the major milestones in the evolution of computing.","resultHTML":"<h1 id=\"md-12281wm-368-k1olys-lecture-1-computing-concepts\" mainmatter=\"start\">Lecture 1 – Computing Concepts</h1>\n<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-368-k1olys-learning-objectives\">Learning Objectives</h2>\n<p>At the end of this chapter, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Define what a computer is.\n</li>\n<li>Distinguish between hardware and software.\n</li>\n<li>Explain the input-process-output-storage model.\n</li>\n<li>Differentiate between general-purpose computers and embedded systems.\n</li>\n<li>Explain the concept of abstraction in computing.\n</li>\n<li>Describe the major milestones in the evolution of computing.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"568f5331b8aedda476ceae30fa920e8514233182192a6e934821d20f1451dbdc","markdown":"{mainmatter=\"start\"}\n# Lecture 1 – Computerconcepten\n\n## Leerdoelen\n\nAan het einde van dit hoofdstuk moeten studenten in staat zijn om:\n\n- Definiëren wat een computer is.\n- Onderscheid maken tussen hardware en software.\n- Het invoer-verwerking-uitvoer-opslagmodel uitleggen.\n- Onderscheid maken tussen algemene computers en embedded systemen.\n- Het begrip abstractie in de informatica uitleggen.\n- De belangrijkste mijlpalen in de evolutie van de informatica beschrijven."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"568f5331b8aedda476ceae30fa920e8514233182192a6e934821d20f1451dbdc","markdown":"{mainmatter=\"start\"}\n# Cours 1 – Concepts informatiques\n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage\n\nÀ la fin de ce chapitre, les étudiant·e·s devraient être capables de :\n\n- Définir ce qu'est un ordinateur.\n- Distinguer le matériel (hardware) du logiciel (software).\n- Expliquer le modèle entrée–traitement–sortie–stockage.\n- Différencier les ordinateurs à usage général des systèmes embarqués.\n- Expliquer le concept d'abstraction en informatique.\n- Décrire les principales étapes de l'évolution de l'informatique."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"568f5331b8aedda476ceae30fa920e8514233182192a6e934821d20f1451dbdc","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction\n\nComputers are among the most important technologies of modern society.\n\nThey are used in:\n\n- Communication\n- Transportation\n- Healthcare\n- Education\n- Entertainment\n- Scientific research\n- Business and finance\n\nWhen most people hear the word *computer*, they think of a laptop or desktop machine.\n\nHowever, computers exist in many forms:\n\n- Smartphones\n- Smartwatches\n- Cars\n- ATMs\n- Game consoles\n- Smart TVs\n- Home appliances\n- Industrial robots\n\nIn fact, a typical student may interact with dozens of computers every day without realizing it.","output":"","result":"## Introduction\n\nComputers are among the most important technologies of modern society.\n\nThey are used in:\n\n- Communication\n- Transportation\n- Healthcare\n- Education\n- Entertainment\n- Scientific research\n- Business and finance\n\nWhen most people hear the word *computer*, they think of a laptop or desktop machine.\n\nHowever, computers exist in many forms:\n\n- Smartphones\n- Smartwatches\n- Cars\n- ATMs\n- Game consoles\n- Smart TVs\n- Home appliances\n- Industrial robots\n\nIn fact, a typical student may interact with dozens of computers every day without realizing it.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-369-19dqqe5-introduction\">Introduction</h2>\n<p>Computers are among the most important technologies of modern society.</p>\n<p>They are used in:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Communication\n</li>\n<li>Transportation\n</li>\n<li>Healthcare\n</li>\n<li>Education\n</li>\n<li>Entertainment\n</li>\n<li>Scientific research\n</li>\n<li>Business and finance\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When most people hear the word <em>computer</em>, they think of a laptop or desktop machine.</p>\n<p>However, computers exist in many forms:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Smartphones\n</li>\n<li>Smartwatches\n</li>\n<li>Cars\n</li>\n<li>ATMs\n</li>\n<li>Game consoles\n</li>\n<li>Smart TVs\n</li>\n<li>Home appliances\n</li>\n<li>Industrial robots\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>In fact, a typical student may interact with dozens of computers every day without realizing it.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c10cb475b8e68b3bfbb3e9523c3a5c8997fe19f478817fc72587e13703a9e2a0","markdown":"## Inleiding\n\nComputers behoren tot de belangrijkste technologieën van de moderne samenleving.\n\nZe worden gebruikt in:\n\n- Communicatie\n- Vervoer\n- Gezondheidszorg\n- Onderwijs\n- Vermaak\n- Wetenschappelijk onderzoek\n- Bedrijfsleven en financiën\n\nAls de meeste mensen het woord *computer* horen, denken ze aan een laptop of desktopcomputer.\n\nComputers komen echter in veel vormen voor:\n\n- Smartphones\n- Smartwatches\n- Auto's\n- Geldautomaten\n- Spelconsoles\n- Smart-tv's\n- Huishoudelijke apparaten\n- Industriële robots\n\nIn feite kan een gemiddelde student elke dag met tientallen computers in aanraking komen zonder het te beseffen."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c10cb475b8e68b3bfbb3e9523c3a5c8997fe19f478817fc72587e13703a9e2a0","markdown":"## Introduction\n\nLes ordinateurs figurent parmi les technologies les plus importantes de la société moderne.\n\nIls sont utilisés pour :\n\n- Communication\n- Transport\n- Santé\n- Éducation\n- Divertissement\n- Recherche scientifique\n- Affaires et finance\n\nLorsque la plupart des gens entendent le mot *ordinateur*, ils pensent à un ordinateur portable ou de bureau.\n\nCependant, les ordinateurs existent sous de nombreuses formes :\n\n- Smartphones\n- Montres intelligentes\n- Voitures\n- Distributeurs automatiques de billets (DAB)\n- Consoles de jeu\n- Téléviseurs intelligents\n- Appareils électroménagers\n- Robots industriels\n\nEn fait, un étudiant typique peut interagir avec des dizaines d'ordinateurs chaque jour sans s'en rendre compte."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"c10cb475b8e68b3bfbb3e9523c3a5c8997fe19f478817fc72587e13703a9e2a0","language":"English"}},{"input":"## What Is a Computer?\n\n### Definition\n\nA computer is a programmable machine that receives data, processes it according to instructions, produces results, and often stores information for future use.\n\nA simplified model is:\n\n```text\nInput → Processing → Output\n            ↑↓\n         Storage\n```\n\nAll computers, regardless of shape or size, perform these four basic functions.\n\n### Input\n\nInput is information entering the computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Typing on a keyboard\n- Clicking a mouse\n- Touching a smartphone screen\n- Speaking into a microphone\n- Reading data from a sensor\n\n### Processing\n\nProcessing is the transformation of input into useful information.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Calculating a result\n- Editing an image\n- Searching a database\n- Finding a route on a map\n\n### Output\n\nOutput is information produced by the computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Displaying text\n- Playing music\n- Printing a document\n- Showing a web page\n\n### Storage\n\nStorage allows information to be retained.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Documents\n- Photos\n- Videos\n- Installed applications\n\nStorage enables computers to remember information after they are powered off.\n\n### Example: Online Navigation\n\nSuppose you request directions to Brussels.\n\n#### Input\n\n- Current location\n- Destination\n\n#### Processing\n\n- Route calculation\n- Traffic analysis\n\n#### Output\n\n- Directions\n- Travel time\n- Map display\n\n#### Storage\n\n- Saved locations\n- Route history\n\nThis simple example demonstrates all four functions of a computer.","output":"","result":"## What Is a Computer?\n\n### Definition\n\nA computer is a programmable machine that receives data, processes it according to instructions, produces results, and often stores information for future use.\n\nA simplified model is:\n\n```text\nInput → Processing → Output\n            ↑↓\n         Storage\n```\n\nAll computers, regardless of shape or size, perform these four basic functions.\n\n### Input\n\nInput is information entering the computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Typing on a keyboard\n- Clicking a mouse\n- Touching a smartphone screen\n- Speaking into a microphone\n- Reading data from a sensor\n\n### Processing\n\nProcessing is the transformation of input into useful information.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Calculating a result\n- Editing an image\n- Searching a database\n- Finding a route on a map\n\n### Output\n\nOutput is information produced by the computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Displaying text\n- Playing music\n- Printing a document\n- Showing a web page\n\n### Storage\n\nStorage allows information to be retained.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Documents\n- Photos\n- Videos\n- Installed applications\n\nStorage enables computers to remember information after they are powered off.\n\n### Example: Online Navigation\n\nSuppose you request directions to Brussels.\n\n#### Input\n\n- Current location\n- Destination\n\n#### Processing\n\n- Route calculation\n- Traffic analysis\n\n#### Output\n\n- Directions\n- Travel time\n- Map display\n\n#### Storage\n\n- Saved locations\n- Route history\n\nThis simple example demonstrates all four functions of a computer.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-what-is-a-computer\">What Is a Computer?</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-definition\">Definition</h3>\n<p>A computer is a programmable machine that receives data, processes it according to instructions, produces results, and often stores information for future use.</p>\n<p>A simplified model is:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Input → Processing → Output\n            ↑↓\n         Storage</code></pre>\n<p>All computers, regardless of shape or size, perform these four basic functions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-input\">Input</h3>\n<p>Input is information entering the computer.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Typing on a keyboard\n</li>\n<li>Clicking a mouse\n</li>\n<li>Touching a smartphone screen\n</li>\n<li>Speaking into a microphone\n</li>\n<li>Reading data from a sensor\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-processing\">Processing</h3>\n<p>Processing is the transformation of input into useful information.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Calculating a result\n</li>\n<li>Editing an image\n</li>\n<li>Searching a database\n</li>\n<li>Finding a route on a map\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-output\">Output</h3>\n<p>Output is information produced by the computer.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Displaying text\n</li>\n<li>Playing music\n</li>\n<li>Printing a document\n</li>\n<li>Showing a web page\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-storage\">Storage</h3>\n<p>Storage allows information to be retained.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Documents\n</li>\n<li>Photos\n</li>\n<li>Videos\n</li>\n<li>Installed applications\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Storage enables computers to remember information after they are powered off.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-example-online-navigation\">Example: Online Navigation</h3>\n<p>Suppose you request directions to Brussels.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-input-1\">Input</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Current location\n</li>\n<li>Destination\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-processing-1\">Processing</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Route calculation\n</li>\n<li>Traffic analysis\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-output-1\">Output</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Directions\n</li>\n<li>Travel time\n</li>\n<li>Map display\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-370-16qbq9f-storage-1\">Storage</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Saved locations\n</li>\n<li>Route history\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This simple example demonstrates all four functions of a computer.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"5691247ca6d3a15c70ebcd91c9a91382f89295433fe0f0b3c0743cef7711b6ae","markdown":"## Wat is een computer?\n\n### Definitie\n\nEen computer is een programmeerbare machine die gegevens ontvangt, deze volgens instructies verwerkt, resultaten produceert en vaak informatie opslaat voor later gebruik.\n\nEen vereenvoudigd model is:\n\n```text\nInput → Processing → Output\n            ↑↓\n         Storage\n```\n\nAlle computers, ongeacht vorm of grootte, voeren deze vier basisfuncties uit.\n\n### Invoer\n\nInvoer is informatie die de computer binnenkomt.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Typen op een toetsenbord\n- Klikken met een muis\n- Aanraken van een smartphone-scherm\n- Spreken in een microfoon\n- Gegevens lezen van een sensor\n\n### Verwerking\n\nVerwerking is de transformatie van invoer naar bruikbare informatie.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Een resultaat berekenen\n- Een afbeelding bewerken\n- Een database doorzoeken\n- Een route op een kaart vinden\n\n### Uitvoer\n\nUitvoer is informatie die door de computer wordt geproduceerd.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Tekst weergeven\n- Muziek afspelen\n- Een document afdrukken\n- Een webpagina tonen\n\n### Opslag\n\nOpslag maakt het mogelijk informatie te bewaren.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Documenten\n- Foto's\n- Video's\n- Geïnstalleerde applicaties\n\nOpslag stelt computers in staat informatie te onthouden nadat ze zijn uitgeschakeld.\n\n### Voorbeeld: Online navigatie\n\nStel dat je routebeschrijving naar Brussel aanvraagt.\n\n#### Invoer\n\n- Huidige locatie\n- Bestemming\n\n#### Verwerking\n\n- Routeberekening\n- Verkeersanalyse\n\n#### Uitvoer\n\n- Routebeschrijving\n- Reistijd\n- Kaartweergave\n\n#### Opslag\n\n- Opgeslagen locaties\n- Routeregeschiedenis\n\nDit eenvoudige voorbeeld toont alle vier functies van een computer."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"5691247ca6d3a15c70ebcd91c9a91382f89295433fe0f0b3c0743cef7711b6ae","markdown":"## Qu'est-ce qu'un ordinateur?\n\n### Définition\n\nUn ordinateur est une machine programmable qui reçoit des données, les traite selon des instructions, produit des résultats et stocke souvent des informations pour un usage ultérieur.\n\nUn modèle simplifié est :\n\n```text\nInput → Processing → Output\n            ↑↓\n         Storage\n```\n\nTous les ordinateurs, quelle que soit leur forme ou leur taille, accomplissent ces quatre fonctions de base.\n\n### Entrée\n\nL'entrée est l'information qui entre dans l'ordinateur.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Taper au clavier\n- Cliquer avec une souris\n- Toucher l'écran d'un smartphone\n- Parler dans un microphone\n- Lire des données depuis un capteur\n\n### Traitement\n\nLe traitement est la transformation des entrées en informations utiles.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Calculer un résultat\n- Retoucher une image\n- Rechercher dans une base de données\n- Trouver un itinéraire sur une carte\n\n### Sortie\n\nLa sortie est l'information produite par l'ordinateur.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Afficher du texte\n- Jouer de la musique\n- Imprimer un document\n- Afficher une page web\n\n### Stockage\n\nLe stockage permet de conserver l'information.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Documents\n- Photos\n- Vidéos\n- Applications installées\n\nLe stockage permet aux ordinateurs de se souvenir des informations même lorsqu'ils sont éteints.\n\n### Exemple : Navigation en ligne\n\nSupposons que vous demandiez un itinéraire vers Bruxelles.\n\n#### Entrée\n\n- Position actuelle\n- Destination\n\n#### Traitement\n\n- Calcul de l'itinéraire\n- Analyse du trafic\n\n#### Sortie\n\n- Instructions\n- Durée du trajet\n- Affichage de la carte\n\n#### Stockage\n\n- Lieux enregistrés\n- Historique des itinéraires\n\nCet exemple simple illustre les quatre fonctions d'un ordinateur."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"5691247ca6d3a15c70ebcd91c9a91382f89295433fe0f0b3c0743cef7711b6ae","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Hardware and Software\n\nA computer system consists of two major elements:\n\n```text\nHardware\n+\nSoftware\n=\nComputer System\n```\n\n### Hardware\n\nHardware refers to the physical components of a computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Processor\n- Memory\n- Storage devices\n- Display\n- Keyboard\n- Network card\n\nHardware can be touched and physically examined.\n\n### Software\n\nSoftware consists of instructions that tell hardware what to do.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Microsoft Word\n- Google Chrome\n- Mobile applications\n\nSoftware cannot be touched physically. It exists as digital information stored inside computer systems.\n\n### Analogy\n\nConsider a music player.\n\n#### Hardware\n\n- Speakers\n- Buttons\n- Battery\n- Screen\n\n#### Software\n\n- The program that plays music\n\nWithout software, the hardware does nothing useful. Without hardware, the software cannot run.\n\n### Important Observation\n\nThe same hardware can perform very different tasks simply by changing the software.\n\nFor example, the same smartphone can be used for:\n\n- Navigation\n- Banking\n- Gaming\n- Messaging\n- Photography\n\nThe hardware remains largely unchanged. The software determines the behavior.","output":"","result":"## Hardware and Software\n\nA computer system consists of two major elements:\n\n```text\nHardware\n+\nSoftware\n=\nComputer System\n```\n\n### Hardware\n\nHardware refers to the physical components of a computer.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Processor\n- Memory\n- Storage devices\n- Display\n- Keyboard\n- Network card\n\nHardware can be touched and physically examined.\n\n### Software\n\nSoftware consists of instructions that tell hardware what to do.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Microsoft Word\n- Google Chrome\n- Mobile applications\n\nSoftware cannot be touched physically. It exists as digital information stored inside computer systems.\n\n### Analogy\n\nConsider a music player.\n\n#### Hardware\n\n- Speakers\n- Buttons\n- Battery\n- Screen\n\n#### Software\n\n- The program that plays music\n\nWithout software, the hardware does nothing useful. Without hardware, the software cannot run.\n\n### Important Observation\n\nThe same hardware can perform very different tasks simply by changing the software.\n\nFor example, the same smartphone can be used for:\n\n- Navigation\n- Banking\n- Gaming\n- Messaging\n- Photography\n\nThe hardware remains largely unchanged. The software determines the behavior.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-hardware-and-software\">Hardware and Software</h2>\n<p>A computer system consists of two major elements:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Hardware\n+\nSoftware\n=\nComputer System</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-hardware\">Hardware</h3>\n<p>Hardware refers to the physical components of a computer.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Processor\n</li>\n<li>Memory\n</li>\n<li>Storage devices\n</li>\n<li>Display\n</li>\n<li>Keyboard\n</li>\n<li>Network card\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Hardware can be touched and physically examined.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-software\">Software</h3>\n<p>Software consists of instructions that tell hardware what to do.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows\n</li>\n<li>Linux\n</li>\n<li>macOS\n</li>\n<li>Microsoft Word\n</li>\n<li>Google Chrome\n</li>\n<li>Mobile applications\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Software cannot be touched physically. It exists as digital information stored inside computer systems.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Consider a music player.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-hardware-1\">Hardware</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Speakers\n</li>\n<li>Buttons\n</li>\n<li>Battery\n</li>\n<li>Screen\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-software-1\">Software</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>The program that plays music\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Without software, the hardware does nothing useful. Without hardware, the software cannot run.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-371-gt9fnz-important-observation\">Important Observation</h3>\n<p>The same hardware can perform very different tasks simply by changing the software.</p>\n<p>For example, the same smartphone can be used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Navigation\n</li>\n<li>Banking\n</li>\n<li>Gaming\n</li>\n<li>Messaging\n</li>\n<li>Photography\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The hardware remains largely unchanged. The software determines the behavior.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"ece737ac590bdc7b9cd6914080f182c55dfa7a752472390f100ec9d1be8150bb","markdown":"## Hardware en Software\n\nEen computersysteem bestaat uit twee hoofdonderdelen:\n\n```text\nHardware\n+\nSoftware\n=\nComputer System\n```\n\n### Hardware\n\nHardware verwijst naar de fysieke componenten van een computer.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Processor\n- Geheugen\n- Opslagapparaten\n- Scherm\n- Toetsenbord\n- Netwerkkaart\n\nHardware kan worden aangeraakt en fysiek onderzocht.\n\n### Software\n\nSoftware bestaat uit instructies die de hardware vertellen wat te doen.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Microsoft Word\n- Google Chrome\n- Mobiele applicaties\n\nSoftware kan niet fysiek worden aangeraakt. Het bestaat als digitale informatie die in computersystemen is opgeslagen.\n\n### Analogie\n\nBeschouw een muziekspeler.\n\n#### Hardware\n\n- Luidsprekers\n- Knoppen\n- Batterij\n- Scherm\n\n#### Software\n\n- Het programma dat muziek afspeelt\n\nZonder software doet de hardware niets nuttigs. Zonder hardware kan de software niet draaien.\n\n### Belangrijke observatie\n\nDezelfde hardware kan heel verschillende taken uitvoeren door alleen de software te veranderen.\n\nBijvoorbeeld, dezelfde smartphone kan worden gebruikt voor:\n\n- Navigatie\n- Bankieren\n- Gamen\n- Berichtenverkeer\n- Fotografie\n\nDe hardware blijft grotendeels ongewijzigd. De software bepaalt het gedrag."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"ece737ac590bdc7b9cd6914080f182c55dfa7a752472390f100ec9d1be8150bb","markdown":"## Matériel et logiciel\n\nUn système informatique se compose de deux éléments principaux :\n\n```text\nHardware\n+\nSoftware\n=\nComputer System\n```\n\n### Matériel\n\nLe matériel désigne les composants physiques d'un ordinateur.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Processeur\n- Mémoire\n- Dispositifs de stockage\n- Écran\n- Clavier\n- Carte réseau\n\nLe matériel peut être touché et examiné physiquement.\n\n### Logiciel\n\nLe logiciel se compose d'instructions qui indiquent au matériel quoi faire.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Microsoft Word\n- Google Chrome\n- Applications mobiles\n\nLe logiciel ne peut pas être touché physiquement. Il existe sous forme d'informations numériques stockées dans les systèmes informatiques.\n\n### Analogie\n\nConsidérons un lecteur de musique.\n\n#### Matériel\n\n- Enceintes\n- Boutons\n- Batterie\n- Écran\n\n#### Logiciel\n\n- Le programme qui lit la musique\n\nSans logiciel, le matériel ne fait rien d'utile. Sans matériel, le logiciel ne peut pas s'exécuter.\n\n### Observation importante\n\nUn même matériel peut accomplir des tâches très différentes simplement en changeant le logiciel.\n\nPar exemple, le même smartphone peut être utilisé pour :\n\n- Navigation\n- Services bancaires\n- Jeux\n- Messagerie\n- Photographie\n\nLe matériel reste en grande partie inchangé. Le logiciel détermine le comportement."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"ece737ac590bdc7b9cd6914080f182c55dfa7a752472390f100ec9d1be8150bb","language":"English"}},{"input":"## General-Purpose and Embedded Systems\n\nNot all computers are designed for the same purpose.\n\n### General-Purpose Computers\n\nGeneral-purpose computers can perform many different tasks.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Laptops\n- Desktop PCs\n- Smartphones\n- Tablets\n\nUsers can install and remove software as needed.\n\n### Embedded Systems\n\nAn embedded system is a computer designed for a specific purpose.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Microwave oven controller\n- Washing machine controller\n- Traffic lights\n- Card payment terminals\n- Smart thermostats\n\nThese computers focus on a limited set of tasks.\n\n### Comparison\n\n#### General-Purpose Computer\n\n- Many applications\n- Flexible\n- User-controlled\n\nExample: Laptop\n\n#### Embedded System\n\n- Specific purpose\n- Fixed functionality\n- Often invisible to users\n\nExample: Digital thermostat","output":"","result":"## General-Purpose and Embedded Systems\n\nNot all computers are designed for the same purpose.\n\n### General-Purpose Computers\n\nGeneral-purpose computers can perform many different tasks.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Laptops\n- Desktop PCs\n- Smartphones\n- Tablets\n\nUsers can install and remove software as needed.\n\n### Embedded Systems\n\nAn embedded system is a computer designed for a specific purpose.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Microwave oven controller\n- Washing machine controller\n- Traffic lights\n- Card payment terminals\n- Smart thermostats\n\nThese computers focus on a limited set of tasks.\n\n### Comparison\n\n#### General-Purpose Computer\n\n- Many applications\n- Flexible\n- User-controlled\n\nExample: Laptop\n\n#### Embedded System\n\n- Specific purpose\n- Fixed functionality\n- Often invisible to users\n\nExample: Digital thermostat","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-general-purpose-and-embedded-systems\">General-Purpose and Embedded Systems</h2>\n<p>Not all computers are designed for the same purpose.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-general-purpose-computers\">General-Purpose Computers</h3>\n<p>General-purpose computers can perform many different tasks.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptops\n</li>\n<li>Desktop PCs\n</li>\n<li>Smartphones\n</li>\n<li>Tablets\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Users can install and remove software as needed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-embedded-systems\">Embedded Systems</h3>\n<p>An embedded system is a computer designed for a specific purpose.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Microwave oven controller\n</li>\n<li>Washing machine controller\n</li>\n<li>Traffic lights\n</li>\n<li>Card payment terminals\n</li>\n<li>Smart thermostats\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These computers focus on a limited set of tasks.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-comparison\">Comparison</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-general-purpose-computer\">General-Purpose Computer</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Many applications\n</li>\n<li>Flexible\n</li>\n<li>User-controlled\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Example: Laptop</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-12281wm-372-1oiq8m0-embedded-system\">Embedded System</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Specific purpose\n</li>\n<li>Fixed functionality\n</li>\n<li>Often invisible to users\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Example: Digital thermostat</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"fe547544afb7bfcdbd894e2e4251fa91c51f23092df4963fbb8a72e534da7f10","markdown":"## Algemeen inzetbare en ingebedde systemen\n\nNiet alle computers zijn ontworpen voor hetzelfde doel.\n\n### Algemeen inzetbare computers\n\nAlgemeen inzetbare computers kunnen veel verschillende taken uitvoeren.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Laptops\n- Desktop-pc's\n- Smartphones\n- Tablets\n\nGebruikers kunnen naar behoefte software installeren en verwijderen.\n\n### Ingebedde systemen\n\nEen ingebed systeem is een computer die voor een specifiek doel is ontworpen.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Regelaar van een magnetron\n- Regelaar van een wasmachine\n- Verkeerslichten\n- Betaalterminals (pinapparaten)\n- Slimme thermostaten\n\nDeze computers zijn gericht op een beperkte set taken.\n\n### Vergelijking\n\n#### Algemeen inzetbare computer\n\n- Veel toepassingen\n- Flexibel\n- Onder gebruikerscontrole\n\nVoorbeeld: laptop\n\n#### Ingebed systeem\n\n- Specifiek doel\n- Vaste functionaliteit\n- Vaak onzichtbaar voor gebruikers\n\nVoorbeeld: digitale thermostaat"},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"fe547544afb7bfcdbd894e2e4251fa91c51f23092df4963fbb8a72e534da7f10","markdown":"## Ordinateurs à usage général et systèmes embarqués\n\nTous les ordinateurs ne sont pas conçus pour le même usage.\n\n### Ordinateurs à usage général\n\nLes ordinateurs à usage général peuvent effectuer de nombreuses tâches différentes.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Ordinateurs portables\n- Ordinateurs de bureau\n- Smartphones\n- Tablettes\n\nLes utilisateurs peuvent installer et désinstaller des logiciels selon leurs besoins.\n\n### Systèmes embarqués\n\nUn système embarqué est un ordinateur conçu pour un objectif spécifique.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Contrôleur de four micro-ondes\n- Contrôleur de machine à laver\n- Feux de circulation\n- Terminaux de paiement par carte\n- Thermostats intelligents\n\nCes ordinateurs se concentrent sur un ensemble limité de tâches.\n\n### Comparaison\n\n#### Ordinateur à usage général\n\n- De nombreuses applications\n- Polyvalent\n- Contrôlé par l'utilisateur\n\nExemple : Ordinateur portable\n\n#### Système embarqué\n\n- Objectif spécifique\n- Fonctionnalité fixe\n- Souvent invisible pour les utilisateurs\n\nExemple : Thermostat numérique"}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"fe547544afb7bfcdbd894e2e4251fa91c51f23092df4963fbb8a72e534da7f10","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Levels of Abstraction\n\n### Why Abstraction Is Necessary\n\nModern computers are extremely complex. No single person understands every detail simultaneously.\n\nAbstraction allows us to manage complexity by organizing systems into layers. Each layer hides details from the layers above it.\n\n### Everyday Example: Driving a Car\n\nMost drivers know:\n\n- Accelerator\n- Brake\n- Steering wheel\n\nThey do not need to understand:\n\n- Combustion\n- Fuel injection\n- Gearbox mechanics\n\nThe car hides complexity. This is abstraction.\n\n### Abstraction in Computing\n\nWhen writing a document:\n\n```text\nUser\n↓\nWord Processor\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysics\n```\n\nMost users only interact with the top layer. The lower layers work automatically.\n\n### Why Abstraction Matters\n\nWithout abstraction:\n\n- Software development would be extremely difficult.\n- Modern systems would be impossible to manage.\n- Innovation would be much slower.\n\nAbstraction allows specialists to focus on a particular layer.\n\n### Example\n\nA website developer does not need to understand:\n\n- Semiconductor fabrication\n- Electrical engineering\n- Processor design\n\nThe lower layers are hidden through abstraction.","output":"","result":"## Levels of Abstraction\n\n### Why Abstraction Is Necessary\n\nModern computers are extremely complex. No single person understands every detail simultaneously.\n\nAbstraction allows us to manage complexity by organizing systems into layers. Each layer hides details from the layers above it.\n\n### Everyday Example: Driving a Car\n\nMost drivers know:\n\n- Accelerator\n- Brake\n- Steering wheel\n\nThey do not need to understand:\n\n- Combustion\n- Fuel injection\n- Gearbox mechanics\n\nThe car hides complexity. This is abstraction.\n\n### Abstraction in Computing\n\nWhen writing a document:\n\n```text\nUser\n↓\nWord Processor\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysics\n```\n\nMost users only interact with the top layer. The lower layers work automatically.\n\n### Why Abstraction Matters\n\nWithout abstraction:\n\n- Software development would be extremely difficult.\n- Modern systems would be impossible to manage.\n- Innovation would be much slower.\n\nAbstraction allows specialists to focus on a particular layer.\n\n### Example\n\nA website developer does not need to understand:\n\n- Semiconductor fabrication\n- Electrical engineering\n- Processor design\n\nThe lower layers are hidden through abstraction.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-levels-of-abstraction\">Levels of Abstraction</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-why-abstraction-is-necessary\">Why Abstraction Is Necessary</h3>\n<p>Modern computers are extremely complex. No single person understands every detail simultaneously.</p>\n<p>Abstraction allows us to manage complexity by organizing systems into layers. Each layer hides details from the layers above it.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-everyday-example-driving-a-car\">Everyday Example: Driving a Car</h3>\n<p>Most drivers know:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Accelerator\n</li>\n<li>Brake\n</li>\n<li>Steering wheel\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>They do not need to understand:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Combustion\n</li>\n<li>Fuel injection\n</li>\n<li>Gearbox mechanics\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The car hides complexity. This is abstraction.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-abstraction-in-computing\">Abstraction in Computing</h3>\n<p>When writing a document:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>User\n↓\nWord Processor\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysics</code></pre>\n<p>Most users only interact with the top layer. The lower layers work automatically.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-why-abstraction-matters\">Why Abstraction Matters</h3>\n<p>Without abstraction:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Software development would be extremely difficult.\n</li>\n<li>Modern systems would be impossible to manage.\n</li>\n<li>Innovation would be much slower.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Abstraction allows specialists to focus on a particular layer.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-373-1hjl1q-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>A website developer does not need to understand:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Semiconductor fabrication\n</li>\n<li>Electrical engineering\n</li>\n<li>Processor design\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The lower layers are hidden through abstraction.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"4209c98127fd3905de6c51fa4f38a629d9ff958952ed308c0f60dcf766622df6","markdown":"## Niveaus van abstractie\n\n### Waarom abstractie noodzakelijk is\n\nModerne computers zijn extreem complex. Geen enkel persoon begrijpt tegelijkertijd elk detail.\n\nAbstractie stelt ons in staat complexiteit te beheersen door systemen in lagen te organiseren. Elke laag verbergt details voor de lagen erboven.\n\n### Alledaags voorbeeld: autorijden\n\nDe meeste bestuurders kennen:\n\n- Gaspedaal\n- Rem\n- Stuurwiel\n\nZe hoeven niet te begrijpen:\n\n- Verbranding\n- Brandstofinjectie\n- De mechanica van de versnellingsbak\n\nDe auto verbergt de complexiteit. Dit is abstractie.\n\n### Abstractie in informatica\n\nBij het schrijven van een document:\n\n```text\nUser\n↓\nWord Processor\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysics\n```\n\nDe meeste gebruikers hebben alleen met de bovenste laag te maken. De lagere lagen werken automatisch.\n\n### Waarom abstractie belangrijk is\n\nZonder abstractie:\n\n- Softwareontwikkeling zou extreem moeilijk zijn.\n- Moderne systemen zouden onmogelijk te beheren zijn.\n- Innovatie zou veel langzamer verlopen.\n\nAbstractie stelt specialisten in staat zich op een specifieke laag te concentreren.\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nEen webontwikkelaar hoeft niet te begrijpen:\n\n- Fabricage van halfgeleiders\n- Elektrotechniek\n- Processorontwerp\n\nDe lagere lagen worden door abstractie verborgen."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"4209c98127fd3905de6c51fa4f38a629d9ff958952ed308c0f60dcf766622df6","markdown":"## Niveaux d'abstraction\n\n### Pourquoi l'abstraction est nécessaire\n\nLes ordinateurs modernes sont extrêmement complexes. Aucune personne ne comprend tous les détails en même temps.\n\nL'abstraction nous permet de maîtriser la complexité en organisant les systèmes en couches. Chaque couche cache les détails aux couches supérieures.\n\n### Exemple quotidien : conduire une voiture\n\nLa plupart des conducteurs connaissent :\n\n- Accélérateur\n- Frein\n- Volant\n\nIls n'ont pas besoin de comprendre :\n\n- Combustion\n- Injection de carburant\n- Mécanique de la boîte de vitesses\n\nLa voiture cache la complexité. C'est l'abstraction.\n\n### L'abstraction en informatique\n\nLors de la rédaction d'un document :\n\n```text\nUser\n↓\nWord Processor\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysics\n```\n\nLa plupart des utilisateurs n'interagissent qu'avec la couche supérieure. Les couches inférieures fonctionnent automatiquement.\n\n### Pourquoi l'abstraction est importante\n\nSans abstraction :\n\n- Le développement logiciel serait extrêmement difficile.\n- Les systèmes modernes seraient impossibles à gérer.\n- L'innovation serait beaucoup plus lente.\n\nL'abstraction permet aux spécialistes de se concentrer sur une couche particulière.\n\n### Exemple\n\nUn développeur de site web n'a pas besoin de comprendre :\n\n- Fabrication de semi-conducteurs\n- Génie électrique\n- Conception de processeurs\n\nLes couches inférieures sont masquées par l'abstraction."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"4209c98127fd3905de6c51fa4f38a629d9ff958952ed308c0f60dcf766622df6","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Computing Stack\n\nA useful view of a computer system is the computing stack.\n\n```text\nUsers\n↓\nApplications\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysical Phenomena\n```\n\n### Users\n\nHumans who interact with the system.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Students\n- Employees\n- Customers\n\n### Applications\n\nPrograms performing specific tasks.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Word processors\n- Browsers\n- Games\n\n### Operating System\n\nThe software layer managing the hardware and providing services to applications.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Android\n\n### Hardware\n\nPhysical computing components.\n\nExamples:\n\n- CPU\n- Memory\n- Storage\n\n### Electronics\n\nElectrical circuits that enable digital computation.","output":"","result":"## The Computing Stack\n\nA useful view of a computer system is the computing stack.\n\n```text\nUsers\n↓\nApplications\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysical Phenomena\n```\n\n### Users\n\nHumans who interact with the system.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Students\n- Employees\n- Customers\n\n### Applications\n\nPrograms performing specific tasks.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Word processors\n- Browsers\n- Games\n\n### Operating System\n\nThe software layer managing the hardware and providing services to applications.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Android\n\n### Hardware\n\nPhysical computing components.\n\nExamples:\n\n- CPU\n- Memory\n- Storage\n\n### Electronics\n\nElectrical circuits that enable digital computation.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-the-computing-stack\">The Computing Stack</h2>\n<p>A useful view of a computer system is the computing stack.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Users\n↓\nApplications\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysical Phenomena</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-users\">Users</h3>\n<p>Humans who interact with the system.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Students\n</li>\n<li>Employees\n</li>\n<li>Customers\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-applications\">Applications</h3>\n<p>Programs performing specific tasks.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Word processors\n</li>\n<li>Browsers\n</li>\n<li>Games\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-operating-system\">Operating System</h3>\n<p>The software layer managing the hardware and providing services to applications.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows\n</li>\n<li>Linux\n</li>\n<li>Android\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-hardware\">Hardware</h3>\n<p>Physical computing components.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CPU\n</li>\n<li>Memory\n</li>\n<li>Storage\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-374-19m3akm-electronics\">Electronics</h3>\n<p>Electrical circuits that enable digital computation.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c80a644fe330eb790a35b24fdf605db08579860aa7b019d4a4ecb25aa4eebcc8","markdown":"## De computerstapel\n\nEen nuttige kijk op een computersysteem is de computerstapel.\n\n```text\nUsers\n↓\nApplications\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysical Phenomena\n```\n\n### Gebruikers\n\nMensen die met het systeem interageren.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Studenten\n- Werknemers\n- Klanten\n\n### Applicaties\n\nProgramma's die specifieke taken uitvoeren.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Tekstverwerkers\n- Browsers\n- Spellen\n\n### Besturingssysteem\n\nDe softwarelaag die de hardware beheert en diensten aan applicaties levert.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Android\n\n### Hardware\n\nFysieke computercomponenten.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- CPU\n- Geheugen\n- Opslag\n\n### Elektronica\n\nElektrische schakelingen die digitale berekeningen mogelijk maken."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c80a644fe330eb790a35b24fdf605db08579860aa7b019d4a4ecb25aa4eebcc8","markdown":"## La pile informatique\n\nUne vue utile d'un système informatique est la pile informatique.\n\n```text\nUsers\n↓\nApplications\n↓\nOperating System\n↓\nHardware\n↓\nElectronics\n↓\nPhysical Phenomena\n```\n\n### Utilisateurs\n\nPersonnes qui interagissent avec le système.\n\nExemples:\n\n- Étudiants\n- Employés\n- Clients\n\n### Applications\n\nProgrammes effectuant des tâches spécifiques.\n\nExemples:\n\n- Traitements de texte\n- Navigateurs\n- Jeux\n\n### Système d'exploitation\n\nLa couche logicielle qui gère le matériel et fournit des services aux applications.\n\nExemples:\n\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Android\n\n### Matériel\n\nComposants informatiques physiques.\n\nExemples:\n\n- CPU\n- Mémoire\n- Stockage\n\n### Électronique\n\nCircuits électriques qui permettent le calcul numérique."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"c80a644fe330eb790a35b24fdf605db08579860aa7b019d4a4ecb25aa4eebcc8","language":"English"}},{"input":"## A Brief History of Computing\n\n### Early Computing Tools\n\nHumans have always needed help performing calculations.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- Counting sticks\n- Abacus\n- Mechanical calculators\n\nThese devices assisted with arithmetic but had limited capabilities.\n\n### Mechanical Computing\n\nIn the nineteenth century, engineers envisioned machines capable of performing complex calculations automatically.\n\nThe key idea emerged: A machine could follow a sequence of instructions.\n\nThis concept remains central to computing today.\n\n### Electronic Computing\n\nIn the twentieth century, electronics transformed computation.\n\nBenefits included:\n\n- Higher speed\n- Better reliability\n- Increased automation\n\nEarly computers occupied entire rooms.\n\n### Personal Computing\n\nThe introduction of affordable personal computers made computing available to individuals and small organizations.\n\nPersonal computers enabled:\n\n- Word processing\n- Spreadsheets\n- Electronic communication\n\n### Internet Era\n\nThe Internet connected computers worldwide.\n\nNew possibilities emerged:\n\n- Email\n- Web browsing\n- Online commerce\n- Cloud services\n\n### Mobile Computing\n\nComputing moved into pockets.\n\nModern smartphones combine:\n\n- Communication\n- Navigation\n- Photography\n- Entertainment\n- Internet access\n\nin a single device.","output":"","result":"## A Brief History of Computing\n\n### Early Computing Tools\n\nHumans have always needed help performing calculations.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- Counting sticks\n- Abacus\n- Mechanical calculators\n\nThese devices assisted with arithmetic but had limited capabilities.\n\n### Mechanical Computing\n\nIn the nineteenth century, engineers envisioned machines capable of performing complex calculations automatically.\n\nThe key idea emerged: A machine could follow a sequence of instructions.\n\nThis concept remains central to computing today.\n\n### Electronic Computing\n\nIn the twentieth century, electronics transformed computation.\n\nBenefits included:\n\n- Higher speed\n- Better reliability\n- Increased automation\n\nEarly computers occupied entire rooms.\n\n### Personal Computing\n\nThe introduction of affordable personal computers made computing available to individuals and small organizations.\n\nPersonal computers enabled:\n\n- Word processing\n- Spreadsheets\n- Electronic communication\n\n### Internet Era\n\nThe Internet connected computers worldwide.\n\nNew possibilities emerged:\n\n- Email\n- Web browsing\n- Online commerce\n- Cloud services\n\n### Mobile Computing\n\nComputing moved into pockets.\n\nModern smartphones combine:\n\n- Communication\n- Navigation\n- Photography\n- Entertainment\n- Internet access\n\nin a single device.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-a-brief-history-of-computing\">A Brief History of Computing</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-early-computing-tools\">Early Computing Tools</h3>\n<p>Humans have always needed help performing calculations.</p>\n<p>Examples include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Counting sticks\n</li>\n<li>Abacus\n</li>\n<li>Mechanical calculators\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These devices assisted with arithmetic but had limited capabilities.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-mechanical-computing\">Mechanical Computing</h3>\n<p>In the nineteenth century, engineers envisioned machines capable of performing complex calculations automatically.</p>\n<p>The key idea emerged: A machine could follow a sequence of instructions.</p>\n<p>This concept remains central to computing today.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-electronic-computing\">Electronic Computing</h3>\n<p>In the twentieth century, electronics transformed computation.</p>\n<p>Benefits included:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Higher speed\n</li>\n<li>Better reliability\n</li>\n<li>Increased automation\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Early computers occupied entire rooms.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-personal-computing\">Personal Computing</h3>\n<p>The introduction of affordable personal computers made computing available to individuals and small organizations.</p>\n<p>Personal computers enabled:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Word processing\n</li>\n<li>Spreadsheets\n</li>\n<li>Electronic communication\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-internet-era\">Internet Era</h3>\n<p>The Internet connected computers worldwide.</p>\n<p>New possibilities emerged:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Email\n</li>\n<li>Web browsing\n</li>\n<li>Online commerce\n</li>\n<li>Cloud services\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-375-1tjm0sx-mobile-computing\">Mobile Computing</h3>\n<p>Computing moved into pockets.</p>\n<p>Modern smartphones combine:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Communication\n</li>\n<li>Navigation\n</li>\n<li>Photography\n</li>\n<li>Entertainment\n</li>\n<li>Internet access\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>in a single device.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"8ad4947ef9c323614ca6e43176fd60f1f17bcfac907d20890879607f141df746","markdown":"## Een korte geschiedenis van de informatica\n\n### Vroege rekenhulpmiddelen\n\nMensen hebben altijd hulp nodig gehad bij het uitvoeren van berekeningen.\n\nVoorbeelden zijn:\n\n- Telstokken\n- Abacus\n- Mechanische rekenmachines\n\nDeze apparaten hielpen bij rekenwerk maar hadden beperkte mogelijkheden.\n\n### Mechanisch rekenen\n\nIn de negentiende eeuw voorzagen ingenieurs machines die in staat waren complexe berekeningen automatisch uit te voeren.\n\nHet kernidee ontstond: een machine kon een reeks instructies volgen.\n\nDit concept is nog steeds centraal in de informatica.\n\n### Elektronisch rekenen\n\nIn de twintigste eeuw transformeerde de elektronica het rekenen.\n\nVoordelen waren onder andere:\n\n- Grotere snelheid\n- Betere betrouwbaarheid\n- Meer automatisering\n\nVroege computers namen hele kamers in beslag.\n\n### Persoonlijk computergebruik\n\nDe introductie van betaalbare personal computers maakte computergebruik mogelijk voor individuen en kleine organisaties.\n\nPersonal computers maakten mogelijk:\n\n- Tekstverwerking\n- Spreadsheetprogramma's\n- Elektronische communicatie\n\n### Internettijdperk\n\nHet internet verbond computers wereldwijd.\n\nNieuwe mogelijkheden ontstonden:\n\n- E-mail\n- Websurfen\n- Online handel\n- Clouddiensten\n\n### Mobiel computergebruik\n\nComputergebruik verhuisde naar de zak.\n\nModerne smartphones combineren:\n\n- Communicatie\n- Navigatie\n- Fotografie\n- Entertainment\n- Toegang tot internet\n\nin één apparaat."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"8ad4947ef9c323614ca6e43176fd60f1f17bcfac907d20890879607f141df746","markdown":"## Brève histoire de l'informatique\n\n### Premiers outils de calcul\n\nLes humains ont toujours eu besoin d'aide pour effectuer des calculs.\n\nParmi les exemples :\n\n- Bâtons à compter\n- Boulier\n- Calculatrices mécaniques\n\nCes dispositifs aidaient aux opérations arithmétiques mais avaient des capacités limitées.\n\n### Calcul mécanique\n\nAu XIXe siècle, des ingénieurs ont imaginé des machines capables d'effectuer automatiquement des calculs complexes.\n\nL'idée clé est apparue : une machine pouvait suivre une séquence d'instructions.\n\nCe concept reste au cœur de l'informatique aujourd'hui.\n\n### Informatique électronique\n\nAu XXe siècle, l'électronique a transformé le calcul.\n\nLes avantages comprenaient :\n\n- Une vitesse accrue\n- Une meilleure fiabilité\n- Une automatisation accrue\n\nLes premiers ordinateurs occupaient des salles entières.\n\n### Informatique personnelle\n\nL'arrivée des ordinateurs personnels abordables a rendu l'informatique accessible aux particuliers et aux petites organisations.\n\nLes ordinateurs personnels ont permis :\n\n- Le traitement de texte\n- Les tableurs\n- La communication électronique\n\n### Ère d'Internet\n\nInternet a connecté les ordinateurs dans le monde entier.\n\nDe nouvelles possibilités ont émergé :\n\n- Le courrier électronique\n- La navigation Web\n- Le commerce en ligne\n- Les services cloud\n\n### Informatique mobile\n\nL'informatique s'est glissée dans les poches.\n\nLes smartphones modernes combinent :\n\n- La communication\n- La navigation\n- La photographie\n- Le divertissement\n- L'accès à Internet\n\ndans un seul appareil."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"8ad4947ef9c323614ca6e43176fd60f1f17bcfac907d20890879607f141df746","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Digital Transformation\n\nComputers have changed nearly every sector.\n\n### Communication\n\n- Email\n- Messaging\n- Video conferencing\n\n### Education\n\n- Learning platforms\n- Digital libraries\n- Online courses\n\n### Business\n\n- E-commerce\n- Inventory systems\n- Data analytics\n\n### Healthcare\n\n- Medical imaging\n- Electronic patient records\n- Diagnostic support systems\n\n### Entertainment\n\n- Streaming services\n- Gaming\n- Social media\n\n### Benefits\n\n- Increased productivity\n- Faster communication\n- Global access to information\n\n### Challenges\n\n- Security threats\n- Privacy concerns\n- Dependence on technology\n- Information overload\n\nSeveral of these topics will be revisited later in the course.","output":"","result":"## The Digital Transformation\n\nComputers have changed nearly every sector.\n\n### Communication\n\n- Email\n- Messaging\n- Video conferencing\n\n### Education\n\n- Learning platforms\n- Digital libraries\n- Online courses\n\n### Business\n\n- E-commerce\n- Inventory systems\n- Data analytics\n\n### Healthcare\n\n- Medical imaging\n- Electronic patient records\n- Diagnostic support systems\n\n### Entertainment\n\n- Streaming services\n- Gaming\n- Social media\n\n### Benefits\n\n- Increased productivity\n- Faster communication\n- Global access to information\n\n### Challenges\n\n- Security threats\n- Privacy concerns\n- Dependence on technology\n- Information overload\n\nSeveral of these topics will be revisited later in the course.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-the-digital-transformation\">The Digital Transformation</h2>\n<p>Computers have changed nearly every sector.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-communication\">Communication</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Email\n</li>\n<li>Messaging\n</li>\n<li>Video conferencing\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-education\">Education</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Learning platforms\n</li>\n<li>Digital libraries\n</li>\n<li>Online courses\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-business\">Business</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>E-commerce\n</li>\n<li>Inventory systems\n</li>\n<li>Data analytics\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-healthcare\">Healthcare</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Medical imaging\n</li>\n<li>Electronic patient records\n</li>\n<li>Diagnostic support systems\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-entertainment\">Entertainment</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Streaming services\n</li>\n<li>Gaming\n</li>\n<li>Social media\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-benefits\">Benefits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Increased productivity\n</li>\n<li>Faster communication\n</li>\n<li>Global access to information\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-12281wm-376-l0w4t1-challenges\">Challenges</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Security threats\n</li>\n<li>Privacy concerns\n</li>\n<li>Dependence on technology\n</li>\n<li>Information overload\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Several of these topics will be revisited later in the course.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c96ceaacb8ee169f589e10d0b820a8f964f432e52fd275191397659670466cbf","markdown":"## De digitale transformatie\n\nComputers hebben bijna alle sectoren veranderd.\n\n### Communicatie\n\n- E-mail\n- Berichten\n- Videoconferenties\n\n### Onderwijs\n\n- Leerplatforms\n- Digitale bibliotheken\n- Online cursussen\n\n### Bedrijven\n\n- E-commerce\n- Voorraadsystemen\n- Data-analyse\n\n### Gezondheidszorg\n\n- Medische beeldvorming\n- Elektronische patiëntendossiers\n- Diagnoseondersteunende systemen\n\n### Vermaak\n\n- Streamingdiensten\n- Gamen\n- Sociale media\n\n### Voordelen\n\n- Verhoogde productiviteit\n- Snellere communicatie\n- Wereldwijde toegang tot informatie\n\n### Uitdagingen\n\n- Beveiligingsdreigingen\n- Privacyzorgen\n- Afhankelijkheid van technologie\n- Informatie-overload\n\nVerschillende van deze onderwerpen komen later in de cursus opnieuw aan bod."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c96ceaacb8ee169f589e10d0b820a8f964f432e52fd275191397659670466cbf","markdown":"## La transformation numérique\n\nLes ordinateurs ont transformé presque tous les secteurs.\n\n### Communication\n\n- Courriel\n- Messagerie\n- Vidéoconférence\n\n### Éducation\n\n- Plateformes d'apprentissage\n- Bibliothèques numériques\n- Cours en ligne\n\n### Entreprise\n\n- Commerce électronique\n- Systèmes de gestion des stocks\n- Analyse des données\n\n### Santé\n\n- Imagerie médicale\n- Dossiers patients électroniques\n- Systèmes d'aide au diagnostic\n\n### Divertissement\n\n- Services de streaming\n- Jeux vidéo\n- Réseaux sociaux\n\n### Avantages\n\n- Productivité accrue\n- Communication plus rapide\n- Accès mondial à l'information\n\n### Défis\n\n- Menaces à la sécurité\n- Problèmes de confidentialité\n- Dépendance à la technologie\n- Surcharge d'information\n\nPlusieurs de ces sujets seront repris plus tard dans le cours."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"c96ceaacb8ee169f589e10d0b820a8f964f432e52fd275191397659670466cbf","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Summary\n\nA computer is a programmable machine that performs four fundamental functions:\n\n- Input\n- Processing\n- Output\n- Storage\n\nKey concepts from this chapter:\n\n- Computers are everywhere.\n- Hardware consists of physical components.\n- Software consists of instructions and programs.\n- General-purpose computers can perform many tasks.\n- Embedded systems are designed for specific tasks.\n- Abstraction allows complex systems to be understood through layers.\n- The computing stack links users to hardware.\n- Computing has evolved from simple mechanical tools to globally connected digital systems.","output":"","result":"## Summary\n\nA computer is a programmable machine that performs four fundamental functions:\n\n- Input\n- Processing\n- Output\n- Storage\n\nKey concepts from this chapter:\n\n- Computers are everywhere.\n- Hardware consists of physical components.\n- Software consists of instructions and programs.\n- General-purpose computers can perform many tasks.\n- Embedded systems are designed for specific tasks.\n- Abstraction allows complex systems to be understood through layers.\n- The computing stack links users to hardware.\n- Computing has evolved from simple mechanical tools to globally connected digital systems.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-377-1rfe4gu-summary\">Summary</h2>\n<p>A computer is a programmable machine that performs four fundamental functions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Input\n</li>\n<li>Processing\n</li>\n<li>Output\n</li>\n<li>Storage\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Key concepts from this chapter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computers are everywhere.\n</li>\n<li>Hardware consists of physical components.\n</li>\n<li>Software consists of instructions and programs.\n</li>\n<li>General-purpose computers can perform many tasks.\n</li>\n<li>Embedded systems are designed for specific tasks.\n</li>\n<li>Abstraction allows complex systems to be understood through layers.\n</li>\n<li>The computing stack links users to hardware.\n</li>\n<li>Computing has evolved from simple mechanical tools to globally connected digital systems.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"b305b5edb55d26a1ae7a931afeef6a4a4c60e0e1ee38403acdb92a2d2f6b9ec1","markdown":"## Samenvatting\n\nEen computer is een programmeerbare machine die vier fundamentele functies uitvoert:\n\n- Invoer\n- Verwerking\n- Uitvoer\n- Opslag\n\nBelangrijke begrippen uit dit hoofdstuk:\n\n- Computers zijn overal.\n- Hardware bestaat uit fysieke componenten.\n- Software bestaat uit instructies en programma's.\n- Algemeen inzetbare computers kunnen veel taken uitvoeren.\n- Ingesloten systemen zijn ontworpen voor specifieke taken.\n- Abstractie maakt het mogelijk complexe systemen via lagen te begrijpen.\n- De computing-stack verbindt gebruikers met hardware.\n- De computertechnologie is geëvolueerd van eenvoudige mechanische hulpmiddelen tot wereldwijd verbonden digitale systemen."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"b305b5edb55d26a1ae7a931afeef6a4a4c60e0e1ee38403acdb92a2d2f6b9ec1","markdown":"## Résumé\n\nUn ordinateur est une machine programmable qui exécute quatre fonctions fondamentales :\n\n- Entrée\n- Traitement\n- Sortie\n- Stockage\n\nConcepts clés de ce chapitre :\n\n- Les ordinateurs sont omniprésents.\n- Le matériel se compose de composants physiques.\n- Le logiciel se compose d'instructions et de programmes.\n- Les ordinateurs à usage général peuvent accomplir de nombreuses tâches.\n- Les systèmes embarqués sont conçus pour des tâches spécifiques.\n- L'abstraction permet de comprendre des systèmes complexes par couches.\n- La pile informatique relie les utilisateurs au matériel.\n- L'informatique a évolué d'outils mécaniques simples vers des systèmes numériques connectés à l'échelle mondiale."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"b305b5edb55d26a1ae7a931afeef6a4a4c60e0e1ee38403acdb92a2d2f6b9ec1","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term             | Definition                                      |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Computer         | Programmable machine that processes data        |\n| Hardware         | Physical components of a computer               |\n| Software         | Programs and instructions executed by hardware  |\n| Input            | Information entering a system                   |\n| Processing       | Transformation of data                          |\n| Output           | Information produced by a system                |\n| Storage          | Retention of information                        |\n| Embedded System  | Computer dedicated to a specific task           |\n| Abstraction      | Hiding complexity through layers                |\n| Operating System | Software that manages hardware and applications |","output":"","result":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term             | Definition                                      |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Computer         | Programmable machine that processes data        |\n| Hardware         | Physical components of a computer               |\n| Software         | Programs and instructions executed by hardware  |\n| Input            | Information entering a system                   |\n| Processing       | Transformation of data                          |\n| Output           | Information produced by a system                |\n| Storage          | Retention of information                        |\n| Embedded System  | Computer dedicated to a specific task           |\n| Abstraction      | Hiding complexity through layers                |\n| Operating System | Software that manages hardware and applications |","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-378-2i5juw-key-terms\">Key Terms</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Computer</td><td>Programmable machine that processes data</td></tr><tr><td>Hardware</td><td>Physical components of a computer</td></tr><tr><td>Software</td><td>Programs and instructions executed by hardware</td></tr><tr><td>Input</td><td>Information entering a system</td></tr><tr><td>Processing</td><td>Transformation of data</td></tr><tr><td>Output</td><td>Information produced by a system</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>Retention of information</td></tr><tr><td>Embedded System</td><td>Computer dedicated to a specific task</td></tr><tr><td>Abstraction</td><td>Hiding complexity through layers</td></tr><tr><td>Operating System</td><td>Software that manages hardware and applications</td></tr></tbody></table>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"ea7cdbebaf1d3fbb1c7c8fd8a6a02b60cd55dbb639feecb4c66207cccc2ffff1","markdown":"## Belangrijke termen\n\n| Term             | Definitie                                      |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Computer         | Programmeerbare machine die gegevens verwerkt  |\n| Hardware         | Fysieke onderdelen van een computer            |\n| Software         | Programma's en instructies die door hardware worden uitgevoerd |\n| Invoer           | Informatie die een systeem binnenkomt           |\n| Verwerking       | Transformatie van gegevens                      |\n| Uitvoer          | Informatie die door een systeem wordt geproduceerd |\n| Opslag           | Bewaring van informatie                          |\n| Ingebed systeem  | Computer die aan een specifieke taak is gewijd  |\n| Abstractie       | Complexiteit verbergen via lagen                |\n| Besturingssysteem | Software die hardware en toepassingen beheert   |"},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"ea7cdbebaf1d3fbb1c7c8fd8a6a02b60cd55dbb639feecb4c66207cccc2ffff1","markdown":"## Termes clés\n\n| Terme             | Définition                                      |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Ordinateur         | Machine programmable qui traite des données        |\n| Matériel         | Composants physiques d'un ordinateur               |\n| Logiciel         | Programmes et instructions exécutés par le matériel  |\n| Entrée            | Informations entrant dans un système                   |\n| Traitement       | Transformation des données                          |\n| Sortie           | Informations produites par un système                |\n| Stockage          | Rétention des informations                        |\n| Système embarqué  | Ordinateur dédié à une tâche spécifique           |\n| Abstraction      | Cacher la complexité à travers des couches                |\n| Système d'exploitation | Logiciel qui gère le matériel et les applications |"}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"ea7cdbebaf1d3fbb1c7c8fd8a6a02b60cd55dbb639feecb4c66207cccc2ffff1","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Review Questions\n\n- What are the four fundamental functions of a computer?\n- What is the difference between hardware and software?\n- Give three examples of embedded systems.\n- Why are modern computers dependent on abstraction?\n- What is the role of an operating system?\n- How does a smartphone differ from an embedded system?\n- Describe the layers of the computing stack.\n- Why was the Internet an important milestone in the history of computing?\n- Give two benefits and two challenges of the digital transformation.\n- Explain why a computer can perform many different tasks even if its hardware remains unchanged.","output":"","result":"## Review Questions\n\n- What are the four fundamental functions of a computer?\n- What is the difference between hardware and software?\n- Give three examples of embedded systems.\n- Why are modern computers dependent on abstraction?\n- What is the role of an operating system?\n- How does a smartphone differ from an embedded system?\n- Describe the layers of the computing stack.\n- Why was the Internet an important milestone in the history of computing?\n- Give two benefits and two challenges of the digital transformation.\n- Explain why a computer can perform many different tasks even if its hardware remains unchanged.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-379-1o1x3rt-review-questions\">Review Questions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What are the four fundamental functions of a computer?\n</li>\n<li>What is the difference between hardware and software?\n</li>\n<li>Give three examples of embedded systems.\n</li>\n<li>Why are modern computers dependent on abstraction?\n</li>\n<li>What is the role of an operating system?\n</li>\n<li>How does a smartphone differ from an embedded system?\n</li>\n<li>Describe the layers of the computing stack.\n</li>\n<li>Why was the Internet an important milestone in the history of computing?\n</li>\n<li>Give two benefits and two challenges of the digital transformation.\n</li>\n<li>Explain why a computer can perform many different tasks even if its hardware remains unchanged.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"a1db5d6014f75b2c352ec051df3008efa88becea5dabe5863c8380c5c7205ba9","markdown":"## Herhalingsvragen\n\n- Wat zijn de vier fundamentele functies van een computer?\n- Wat is het verschil tussen hardware en software?\n- Geef drie voorbeelden van embedded systemen.\n- Waarom zijn moderne computers afhankelijk van abstractie?\n- Wat is de rol van een besturingssysteem?\n- Hoe verschilt een smartphone van een embedded systeem?\n- Beschrijf de lagen van de computing-stack.\n- Waarom was het internet een belangrijke mijlpaal in de geschiedenis van de informatica?\n- Geef twee voordelen en twee uitdagingen van de digitale transformatie.\n- Leg uit waarom een computer veel verschillende taken kan uitvoeren, zelfs als de hardware ongewijzigd blijft."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"a1db5d6014f75b2c352ec051df3008efa88becea5dabe5863c8380c5c7205ba9","markdown":"## Questions de révision\n\n- Quelles sont les quatre fonctions fondamentales d'un ordinateur ?\n- Quelle est la différence entre le matériel (hardware) et les logiciels (software) ?\n- Donnez trois exemples de systèmes embarqués.\n- Pourquoi les ordinateurs modernes dépendent-ils de l'abstraction ?\n- Quel est le rôle d'un système d'exploitation ?\n- En quoi un smartphone diffère-t-il d'un système embarqué ?\n- Décrivez les couches de la pile informatique.\n- Pourquoi Internet a-t-il été une étape importante dans l'histoire de l'informatique ?\n- Donnez deux avantages et deux défis de la transformation numérique.\n- Expliquez pourquoi un ordinateur peut effectuer de nombreuses tâches différentes même si son matériel reste inchangé."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"a1db5d6014f75b2c352ec051df3008efa88becea5dabe5863c8380c5c7205ba9","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 2\n\nWe now understand **what a computer is** and **how computing systems are organized**. The next question is:\n\nHow does a computer represent information?\n\nIn Lecture 2, we will discover how text, images, sound, and video are all transformed into binary data composed of bits and bytes.","output":"","result":"## Transition to Lecture 2\n\nWe now understand **what a computer is** and **how computing systems are organized**. The next question is:\n\nHow does a computer represent information?\n\nIn Lecture 2, we will discover how text, images, sound, and video are all transformed into binary data composed of bits and bytes.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-12281wm-380-41srt0-transition-to-lecture-2\">Transition to Lecture 2</h2>\n<p>We now understand <strong>what a computer is</strong> and <strong>how computing systems are organized</strong>. The next question is:</p>\n<p>How does a computer represent information?</p>\n<p>In Lecture 2, we will discover how text, images, sound, and video are all transformed into binary data composed of bits and bytes.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c3f7695d958c63c0c2175fec46c2bbf9a5d10751936194a5b99a6c7509efd2a7","markdown":"## Overgang naar Lezing 2\n\nWe begrijpen nu **wat een computer is** en **hoe computersystemen georganiseerd zijn**. De volgende vraag is:\n\nHoe stelt een computer informatie voor?\n\nIn Lezing 2 zullen we ontdekken hoe tekst, afbeeldingen, geluid en video allemaal worden omgezet in binaire gegevens die bestaan uit bits en bytes."},"French":{"format":1,"sourceHash":"c3f7695d958c63c0c2175fec46c2bbf9a5d10751936194a5b99a6c7509efd2a7","markdown":"## Transition vers la Leçon 2\n\nNous comprenons maintenant **ce qu'est un ordinateur** et **comment les systèmes informatiques sont organisés**. La question suivante est :\n\nComment un ordinateur représente-t-il l'information ?\n\nDans la Leçon 2, nous découvrirons comment le texte, les images, le son et la vidéo sont tous transformés en données binaires composées de bits et d'octets."}},"translationSource":{"sourceHash":"c3f7695d958c63c0c2175fec46c2bbf9a5d10751936194a5b99a6c7509efd2a7","language":"English"}}]